message: "If you use or build on this work, please cite it and credit fgfgfgli."
title: "Canon EOS R1 burst-throttle research"
abstract: "A research note on the Canon EOS R1 burst behaviour: the pause is caused by the front buffer filling up, not by a frame-count quota; rewriting the 'continue' rule into the camera's own suspend path yields a non-blocking 'shoot, pause briefly, continue' behaviour (about 15-20 fps equivalent). Documentation only; no firmware, keys, payloads or tools."
